{"tool_name":"atoll","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"atoll","home":"https://atoll.drugdesign.unistra.fr/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"ATOLL (Aligned Transmembrane dOmain Layout fLattening) is a program for visualizing 3D structures of the transmembrane helix bundle of membrane proteins.","addition_date":"2022-05-18T07:19:27.607173Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-18T07:19:27.610504Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:atoll","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ekellen@unistra.fr","name":"Esther Kellenberger","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9320-4840","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"},{"term":"Protein structure comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2487"},{"term":"Simulation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0244"},{"term":"Transmembrane protein prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0269"},{"term":"Transmembrane protein visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2241"}]}],"name":"ATOLL","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAB860","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 The Author(s) 2021. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.Summary: The 3D structure of transmembrane helices plays a key role in the function of membrane proteins. While visual inspection can usually discern the distinctive features of a helix bundle, simply translating them into a 2D diagram can be difficult. ATOLL (Aligned Transmembrane dOmains Layout fLattening) projects the helix bundle onto the lipid bilayer plane, thereby facilitating the comparison of different structures of the same membrane protein or structures of different membrane proteins.","authors":[{"name":"Bret G."},{"name":"G